  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Karl bought five folders from Pay-A-Lot at a cost of \\(\\$2.50\\) each. Pay-A-Lot had a \\(20\\%\\)-off sale the following day. How much could Karl have saved on the purchase by waiting a day?",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\$ 1.00\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\$ 2.00\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\$ 2.50\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\$ 2.75\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\$ 5.00\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-2005-p2.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Karl paid \\(5\\cdot\\$2.50=\\$12.50\\) for the folders.\n\nA \\(20\\%\\) discount on \\(\\$12.50\\) would save \\(0.20\\cdot12.50=2.50\\) dollars.\n\nThus, C is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Find the total price of the five folders.",
        "The savings would be \\(20\\%\\) of that total."
